Z||000000||Oreif||06-23-2001||12:29 AM||||Below is a pic of the cover I made for all the amps and such behind the passenger seat.<BR>How does it look?<BR>(Note: That is a door emblem painted gray to match the carpeting. It's a "one of a kind"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   )<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/amprak_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Alex2004||06-23-2001||12:32 AM||||That looks REALLY NICE, i like it. Was it hard to make? makes it look neat, and almost factory.<P><BR>Alex...||||reg||10
Z||000002||Oreif||06-23-2001||12:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Alex2004:<BR><B>That looks REALLY NICE, i like it. Was it hard to make? makes it look neat, and almost factory.<P><BR>Alex...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I made it out of a piece of 1/8" paneling and a small strip of wood for the top edge. Then carpeted it. I used paper to trace out the stencil on where to cut the openings at and taped it to the panel to cut.<BR>||||reg||1
