Z||000014||Oreif||06-23-2001||09:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>looks great but doesnt the heat consern you with the back of your seat?<P>Kyle</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>The amps get warm but not hot. They won't do anything to the seats. In my first Fiero I had a set of amps that got hotter than these and they never did anything to the seats.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Tweek||06-23-2001||12:02 PM||||That kicks A$$!!<P>I was looking for a place to put my amp and realized that the centre consol was about the right size....<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/amp0001.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/amp0002.jpg">  <P>The wires that feed it just go right through the grille there...   I would suggedt thought that if anyone else does this, DISCONNECT the + one before feeding it through, the case on the ECM is grounded, I was surprised I didnt kill it.<p>[This message has been edited by Tweek (edited 06-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Seanh||06-23-2001||12:28 PM||||That looks awesome! I am working on somthing similar, well kinda, out of fiberglass right now. Mine will only be housing a pair of MTX amps, one MTX Thunder 500D and one Thunder 302, and an electronic crossover. I am debating if I should put both amps on one side, or one on each side.<P>Oreif, It looks from the pictures that your firewall is even on both sides. Did you make another panel to go behind the drivers side just to make it look even? <P>I wouldn't worry about heat being an issue here. Unless the amps were covered with a plexi-glass panel sealing them in rack, they should have no problem. On my system, I'm going to have the amps under a peice of smoked Lexon, so I'll have a heck of alot of cooling fans on mine. I going to atleast have 4 per amp, and then probally some sucking air and out of the amp rack. Cooler the better (and louder).||||reg||1
